# Repository components published to GitHub Pages by scripts/build-rpm-repo.sh
# and enforced by the in-container collect step.
#
# One line per binary package, whitespace separated:
#   <package>  <component>
#
# Every RPM that rpmbuild produces must have its Name listed here; an unlisted
# package aborts the build so a new subpackage cannot slip in unclassified.
# Which GitHub release an RPM comes from is irrelevant — the split is purely by
# package name.
#
# main   Everything the podman RPM's own Requires resolve to within this
#        repository: podman (+ podman-remote, podman-docker, podmansh) and the
#        version-pinned netavark, aardvark-dns and containers-common(-extra)
#        that core Amazon Linux 2023 does not provide in a new enough version.
# extra  crun, conmon, passt (+ passt-selinux) and catatonit. Core Amazon Linux
#        2023 ships none of them, so on a stock host this component is required
#        too; with the SPAL repository enabled (EPEL9 rebuilds) it becomes
#        optional — SPAL's versions satisfy podman's dependencies and these are
#        the newer upstream builds.
# skip   Built by the upstream spec but never published (test-only and
#        uninstallable-on-AL2023 subpackages). Dropped at collect time.
podman                   main
podman-remote            main
podman-docker            main
podmansh                 main
netavark                 main
aardvark-dns             main
containers-common        main
containers-common-extra  main
crun                     extra
conmon                   extra
passt                    extra
passt-selinux            extra
catatonit                extra
podman-tests             skip
podman-machine           skip
netavark-tests           skip
aardvark-dns-tests       skip
